---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../../assets/images/hero-street-queue.avif";
import SessionsGrid from "../../components/SessionsGrid.astro";
import { navGroups, sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
import NavGroups from "../../components/NavGroups.astro";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={sessionLabels.plural}
  description={`The twelve-week teaching schedule: what happens in each ${sessionLabels.singular.toLowerCase()}, what to prepare, and what leaves the room.`}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="A street in gold and black, a queue of people with backpacks waiting behind a rope barrier along a shopfront under trees, with the road and pavement empty away to the left"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    We call these field sessions rather than tutorials, and the name is doing
    real work. A tutorial is somewhere you sit down and go over the lecture
    again, whereas most of these involve going outside with a stopwatch and
    standing next to something. Two hours a week, usually in the open air, and
    you should assume you will be on your feet for most of it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every session below tells you what to bring and what you are expected to
    walk out with, so please do have a quick look before you turn up. If the
    weather is genuinely awful we move indoors and work on somebody else's
    data instead, and that gets announced on the forum rather than left to
    chance.
  </p>
  <SessionsGrid />

  <NavGroups groups={navGroups} />
</ContentLayout>
